---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
export const prerender = true;

const updated = 'September 28, 2026';
---

<TextPage
  title="Terms of *Service*"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`The rules for using ${SITE.name} (${SITE.domain}) and our free crochet patterns.`}
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>

  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") explain the rules for using {SITE.name} ("we", "us", "our"), available at
    <a href="/">{SITE.domain}</a> (the "Website"). By using the Website, you agree to these Terms. If you do not
    agree, please do not use the Website.
  </p>

  <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Our patterns are <strong>free for your personal use</strong>.</li>
    <li>You <strong>may sell the items you make</strong> from our patterns (small, handmade quantities).</li>
    <li>You <strong>may not copy, share, translate or sell the patterns, text or photos</strong> themselves.</li>
    <li>Please share a <strong>link</strong> to the pattern instead of copying it.</li>
    <li>We work hard to make our patterns accurate, but we can't guarantee they are free of mistakes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="use">1. Using the Website</h2>
  <p>You may use the Website for personal, non-commercial purposes. You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break any law or the rights of others while using the Website;</li>
    <li>try to hack, disrupt, overload or gain unauthorized access to the Website or its systems;</li>
    <li>use bots, scrapers or other automated tools to copy content from the Website;</li>
    <li>send spam, harmful code or abusive messages through our forms.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You must be at least 13 years old (or 16 in the EU) to sign up for the newsletter or contact us. Younger visitors
    should use the Website with a parent or guardian.
  </p>

  <h2 id="patterns">2. Our patterns and content</h2>
  <p>
    All content on the Website – including patterns, written instructions, photos, images, graphics, logos and the
    design of the site – is owned by {SITE.name} and is protected by copyright and other intellectual property laws.
  </p>

  <h3>What you can do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Read, download and print patterns for your own personal use.</li>
    <li>Make as many items as you like from our patterns for yourself, as gifts or for charity.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sell finished items</strong> you have made by hand from our patterns, in small quantities (for example
      at craft fairs or in a small online shop). We kindly ask that you credit {SITE.name} as the pattern designer and
      include a link to <a href="/">{SITE.domain}</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Share photos of your finished makes on social media – we'd love to see them! Please link to the original pattern.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What you can't do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Copy, republish, translate or share our written patterns, in full or in part, on other websites, social media, groups, videos or printed materials.</li>
    <li>Sell, give away or distribute our patterns, including as PDFs, printouts or kits.</li>
    <li>Use our photos or images to sell your own items or promote your own business.</li>
    <li>Claim our patterns or designs as your own.</li>
    <li>Mass-produce items from our patterns in a factory or commercial setting.</li>
    <li>Use our content to train artificial intelligence or machine learning models.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you'd like to use our content in a way not allowed here, please <a href="/contact">ask us first</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="accuracy">3. Pattern accuracy and results</h2>
  <p>
    We test our patterns carefully, but mistakes can happen. Your finished item may also look different from ours
    because of your yarn, hook, tension or skill level. Patterns are provided "as is", and we are not responsible for
    the cost of yarn or materials, or for results that don't match your expectations. If you find an error, please
    <a href="/contact">let us know</a> so we can fix it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="safety">4. Safety</h2>
  <p>You are responsible for making and using your crochet items safely. In particular:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Baby and children's items:</strong> avoid small parts such as buttons, beads or loose ribbons that could
      come off and become a choking hazard. Always supervise babies and young children with handmade items.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Home items:</strong> keep crochet items away from open flames and heat sources.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Items you sell:</strong> if you sell items made from our patterns, you are responsible for following
      any product safety and labeling laws in your country.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="submissions">5. Messages you send us</h2>
  <p>
    When you contact us or share feedback, you confirm that what you send is your own and doesn't break any law. If
    you send us ideas or suggestions, we may use them to improve the Website without owing you anything. We handle
    your personal information as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">6. Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    The Website may contain links to other websites, such as yarn shops or tutorials. We don't control those
    websites and are not responsible for their content, products or privacy practices. Some links may be affiliate
    links, which means we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. We will always make this clear.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimer">7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The Website and all content are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, whether
    express or implied. We do not guarantee that the Website will always be available, secure or free of errors.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent allowed by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential
    damages, or for any loss of materials, time or money, arising from your use of the Website or our patterns. Some
    countries do not allow certain limitations of liability, so some of these limitations may not apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="indemnity">9. Your responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to be responsible for, and to protect {SITE.name} from, any claims that arise from your misuse of the
    Website, your breach of these Terms, or items you make and sell using our patterns.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination">10. Suspension of access</h2>
  <p>
    We may limit or block access to the Website for anyone who breaks these Terms or misuses the Website, without
    notice.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">11. Changes to these Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will change the "Last updated" date at the top of this
    page. By continuing to use the Website after changes are posted, you accept the updated Terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">12. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the country in which {SITE.name} is operated, without regard to its
    conflict of law rules. If any part of these Terms is found to be unenforceable, the rest will remain in effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">13. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about these Terms, please reach out through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
  <p>See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
